<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Jackson Mounds</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1100–1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lake Jackson Mounds are a group of earthen platform mounds on the shore of Lake Jackson, just north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tallahassee">Tallahassee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. Built by people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-walton-culture">Fort Walton culture</a> between about 1100 and 1500, the site was the leading Mississippian ceremonial centre of the region, and burials there yielded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plates and other prestige goods. It is now a Florida state park.</p></div>
